@startuml Grammarly Communication Flows

skinparam ParticipantPadding 10
skinparam BoxPadding 10

box "Browser / Web Page" #LightBlue
  participant "Web Page / Editor" as Page
  participant "Content Script (Grammarly-check/gDocs)" as CS
  participant "Extension UI (Popup / SidePanel)" as UI
end box

box "Extension Background" #LightGreen
  participant "Service Worker (sw.js / Grammarly-bg.js)" as BG
end box

box "Grammarly Cloud Services" #LightPink
  participant "Grammarly Client API (CAPI)" as CAPI
  participant "Auth & Accounts" as Auth
  participant "Telemetry & Metrics" as Metrics
end box

== 1. Initialization and Context Gathering ==
Page -> CS: Interacts / Text Input / DOM Events
CS -> CS: Detect editable elements (Canvas, Iframe, inputs)
CS -> BG: chrome.runtime.sendMessage / connect (channel initialization)
BG -> BG: Cache state (isBGInitialized, feMetricsData)

== 2. Document Checking & Spellcheck (CAPI Loop) ==
CS -> BG: Send document state deltas (submit_ot)
BG -> CAPI: WebSocket (wss://capi.grammarly.com) / API request
CAPI --> BG: Return real-time corrections & suggestions (capiWebSocketMessage)
BG -> CS: Relay corrections/AI suggestions
CS -> Page: Inject UI suggestions / Underlines

== 3. Extension UI Interactions ==
UI -> BG: chrome.runtime.sendMessage (get state / isSidePanelOpen)
BG --> UI: Return account & document state
UI -> BG: Apply suggestions / generative AI trigger
BG -> CAPI: Send generative AI request
CAPI --> BG: Return generated text
BG --> UI: Return generated suggestions

== 4. Telemetry and Analytics ==
BG -> Metrics: Send usage events (https://f-log-extension.grammarly.io, https://gnar.grammarly.com)
CS -> Metrics: Send frontend events (https://femetrics.grammarly.io)

@enduml